%U A401321 298069943878675965988841189,15834609619820513682305329210632,1822117660909170055868341984387852569,451548279262285036147874584034251411604268
%N A401321 Number of strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes that are reducible as a flow graph rooted at some node.
%C A401321 A node h of a strong digraph D is a valid header when the flow graph (D, h) is reducible in the sense of Hecht and Ullman (iterated T1/T2 transformations collapse it to a point); a(n) counts labeled strong digraphs with at least one valid header.
%C A401321 All digraphs here have no self-loops.
%C A401321 For n >= 2, a strongly connected digraph cannot have exactly one valid header.
%C A401321 Let N_j(n) count strongly connected digraphs on n labeled nodes with exactly j valid headers. R_s(n) = number of strong digraphs reducible from every node of a fixed s-subset (independent of the subset by symmetry) satisfies binomial(n,s)*R_s(n) = Sum_j binomial(j,s)*N_j(n); R_1(n) = A397470(n), R_n(n) = A400123(n), and Sum_j N_j(n) = A003030(n).
%D A401321 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A401321 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A401321 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A401321 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A401321 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/b401321.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..30</a>
%H A401321 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A398465/a398465.py.txt">Required Python module (labeled_reducible_cfgs.py)</a>, Jul 2026.
%H A401321 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A400123/a400123_1.py.txt">Required Python module (everywhere_reducible.py)</a>, Sep 2026.
%H A401321 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A401321/a401321_1.py.txt">Python program (valid_header_elections.py)</a>, Oct 2026.
%F A401321 a(n) = Sum_{s=1..n} (-1)^(s+1) * binomial(n,s) * R_s(n) (inclusion-exclusion over root subsets), with R_s as in the comments.
%F A401321 a(n) = A003030(n) - b(n), where b(n) counts strong digraphs reducible from no root.
%F A401321 N_j(n) = Sum_{s>=j} (-1)^(s-j) * binomial(s,j) * binomial(n,s) * R_s(n) (binomial inversion); a(n) = Sum_{j>=1} N_j(n).
%o A401321 (Python)
%o A401321 # Save the three linked Python files in one directory using the filenames
%o A401321 # shown in their link captions, then run Python in that directory.
%o A401321 from valid_header_elections import valid_header_sequence
%o A401321 valid_header_sequence("labeled_strong_some_valid_header", 16)
%Y A401321 Cf. A003030 (all strong digraphs), A397470, A398465, A400123.
